%S A397773 1,3,2,5,3,7,1,1,5,11,6,13,7,15,1,17,1,19,20,63,11,23,3,1,13,1,14,29,
%T A397773 15,31,1,33,17,35,2,37,19,117,10,41,63,43,22,5,23,47,3,1,1,51,52,53,1,
%U A397773 275,7,171,29,59,60,61,31,21,1,65,33,67,68,69,35,71,1,73,37,3,38,77,117,79,10,1
%N A397773 a(n) is the number of distinct values of Sum_{x=0..n-1} exp(2*Pi*i*c*x^n/n^2) as c runs over the residues s^(2*(n-1)) mod n^2 with gcd(s,n) = 1.
%C A397773 #1: a(n) attains every prime number, but it cannot be equal to s^k (k>1) whether s is prime or composite. The 20 most frequently attained nonprime a(n) values (apart from 1) for n<2*10^6 are (171,10,21,63,333,55,68,33,15,164,39,136,26,58,20,6,69,93,1143,275).
%C A397773 #2: a(d) is also the number of distinct values taken by the normalized Gauss sums h(d,s) = g(d, d^2*s^2)/sigma(s), where g(d,n) = Sum_{x mod n} exp(2*Pi*i*x^d/n) and sigma(s) is the product of the local factors: for s = Product p^alpha, writing 2*alpha = q*d + rho with 0 <= rho < d, the factor at p is p^(q*(d-1) + max(rho-1, 0)). For squarefree s, this is simply sigma(s) = s. The reduction to the name above is the identity h(d,s) = d*Sum_{x=0..d-1} exp(2*Pi*i*c*x^d/d^2) with c = s^(2*(d-1)) mod d^2, valid whenever no local rho equals 1. The summand depends only on x mod d, since x^d mod d^2 does; this collapse is what makes the value set finite and small.
%H A397773 Zoltan Reti, <a href="/A397773/b397773.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..10000</a>
%H A397773 Zoltan Reti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21969514">Heilbronn sums as Gaussian periods: the period polynomial, the index, and Wieferich congruences (extended version)</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A397773 Take the prime factorization of n, n = 2^k_0 * Product p_s * Product q_t^k_t where (p_s,q_t are distinct odd primes; here p_s contribute with exponent 1, while k_t >= 2);
%F A397773 Let A:= #{p_s}.
%F A397773   if k_0 = 0 then c:= 1;
%F A397773   if k_0 = 2 then c:= 2^(1-A);
%F A397773   if k_0 = 1 or k_0 = 3,4,...  then c:= 2^(-A).
%F A397773 Then a(n) = c * Product_{unitary prime factors p_s) p_s*gcd(d/p_s, p_s-1).
%t A397773 a[n_] := Module[{f = FactorInteger[n], k = If[OddQ[n], 1, 2], r = If[IntegerExponent[n, 2] == 2, 2, 1]}, Do[If[p[[1]] > 2 && p[[2]] == 1, r *= p[[1]] GCD[n/p[[1]], p[[1]] - 1]/k], {p, f}]; r]
%o A397773 (PARI) a(n) = {my(f=factor(n), k=if(n%2, 1, 2), r=if(valuation(n,2)==2, 2, 1)); for(i=1, #f~, my(p=f[i,1], e=f[i,2]); if(p>2 && e==1, r *= p*gcd(n/p, p-1)/k)); r}
%K A397773 nonn,easy,new
%O A397773 2,2
